  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nDrier mid level air will advect into the region from east to west and\nbreak up cloud cover this afternoon, starting at the issuance of this\nproduct in central Ohio and then working its way westward, reaching\nthe OH/IN/KY border by early evening. This will be the start of a \nprolonged stretch of drier weather.\n\nWhile T/Td spread looks to be unfavorable for fog overnight tonight,\nthe dry air that will be in place will permit radiational cooling\nover sheltered areas, in particular river valleys. Do not see this\nlasting long or being overly dense attm, but future shifts will need\nto look closer at later models to discern this threat. \n\nSynoptically, the Ohio Valley remains on the western periphery of an\nupper level trough, which is driving the cooler/cloudier pattern. We\nwill begin to see a large cut off low develop along the Atlantic \nCoast, creating a blocking pattern through the weekend. This will \nresult in a fairly stagnant weather pattern through the next several \ndays, with a constant advection of some drier air out of the NE. \nThus, a much needed stretch of drier weather conditions are expected,\nalong with temperatures that will trend below seasonal normals.",
